  "interpretation": "<ul data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"1173\">\n<li data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"988\">\n<p data-start=\"779\" data-end=\"832\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">High-resolution (allele-level) HLA typing is used in:</span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"835\" data-end=\"988\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"835\" data-end=\"890\">\n<p data-start=\"837\" data-end=\"890\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"837\" data-end=\"890\">Organ and stem cell transplantation compatibility</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"893\" data-end=\"954\">\n<p data-start=\"895\" data-end=\"954\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"895\" data-end=\"926\">Disease association studies</strong> (e.g. autoimmune disorders)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"957\" data-end=\"988\">\n<p data-start=\"959\" data-end=\"988\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"959\" data-end=\"988\">Pharmacogenetic screening</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"989\" data-end=\"1072\">\n<p data-start=\"991\" data-end=\"1072\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Matching HLA-A, B, and DRB1 alleles is crucial for reducing graft rejection risk.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1073\" data-end=\"1173\">\n<p data-start=\"1075\" data-end=\"1173\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1075\" data-end=\"1093\">HLA mismatches</strong> may increase chances of transplant failure or graft-versus-host disease (GVHD).</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1175\" data-end=\"1351\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1177\" data-end=\"1195\">Fully Matched:</strong> Ideal scenario for donor-recipient matching</span><br data-start=\"1239\" data-end=\"1242\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1245\" data-end=\"1281\">Partially Matched or Mismatched:</strong> May require additional immunosuppression or alternative donor options</span></p>",
